      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the maximum possible area of an equilateral triangle that fits inside a rectangle with sides of lengths 10 and 11, we need to consider the different possible orientations of the equilateral triangle within the rectangle.\n\n### Case 1: The equilateral triangle is oriented with its side along the longer side of the rectangle\nIn this case, the side length of the equilateral triangle is 11. The height \\( h \\) of an equilateral triangle with side length \\( s \\) is given by:\n\\[ h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} s \\]\nFor \\( s = 11 \\):\n\\[ h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 11 = \\frac{11\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\]\nThe triangle can fit within the rectangle as long as the height is less than or equal to 10. Since \\( \\frac{11\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\approx 8.59 \\), which is less than 10, this configuration is valid.\n\nThe area \\( A \\) of an equilateral triangle with side length \\( s \\) is:\n\\[ A = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} s^2 \\]\nFor \\( s = 11 \\):\n\\[ A = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\times 11^2 = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\times 121 = \\frac{121\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\]\n\n### Case 2: The equilateral triangle is oriented with its side along the shorter side of the rectangle\nIn this case, the side length of the equilateral triangle is 10. The height \\( h \\) of an equilateral triangle with side length \\( s \\) is given by:\n\\[ h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} s \\]\nFor \\( s = 10 \\):\n\\[ h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 10 = 5\\sqrt{3} \\]\nThe triangle can fit within the rectangle as long as the height is less than or equal to 11. Since \\( 5\\sqrt{3} \\approx 8.66 \\), which is less than 11, this configuration is also valid.\n\nThe area \\( A \\) of an equilateral triangle with side length \\( s \\) is:\n\\[ A = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} s^2 \\]\nFor \\( s = 10 \\):\n\\[ A = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\times 10^2 = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\times 100 = 25\\sqrt{3} \\]\n\n### Comparing the two cases\nWe need to compare the areas from the two cases:\n\\[ \\frac{121\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\approx 90.95 \\]\n\\[ 25\\sqrt{3} \\approx 43.3 \\]\n\nThe maximum area of the equilateral triangle that fits inside the rectangle is:\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{121\\sqrt{3}}{4}} \\]",
